# ============================================================
# ACLF Early Baseline Survival Prediction - V4 MICE 28/90
# ============================================================
# Study design
#
# Development cohort
#   ├── DEVELOPMENT-only hyperparameter tuning (single 10-fold CV;
#   │      a tuning tool only)
#   ├── fit 4 final base models on FULL development
#   └── External validation cohort (n = 317)
#          └── independent final evaluation (locked pipeline)
#
# Main endpoint:
#   OS     = survival/follow-up time
#   Death  = 1 death, 0 censored
#
# Prediction horizons:
#   28 days / 90 days only
#
# Core models:
#   1. Cox PH
#   2. Elastic Net Cox
#   3. Random Survival Forest
#   4. XGBoost survival
#
# IMPORTANT
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. TEST is locked after the initial split.
# 2. All preprocessing, tuning, model selection, and calibration
#    parameters are learned from DEVELOPMENT only.
# 3. 28/90-day mortality are extracted from survival models;
#    they are not three independent binary models.
# 4. This FIX7 FINAL deliberately avoids ranger formula interface.
# 5. XGBoost survival API varies by package version.
#    This script uses the installed versions shown in your log:
#       R 4.6.1
#       survival 3.8.11
#       glmnet 5.0
#       ranger 0.18.0
#       xgboost 3.2.1.1
# 6. The script stops rather than silently producing invalid metrics
#    when an essential model/API fails.
# ============================================================

